<title>CANADA: Canada Aug natural gas production rises 4.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada Aug natural gas production rises 4.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Tuesday issued the following data for crude oil and natural gas production and exports:</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL AND EQUIVALENT HYDROCARBONS (thousand cubic meters)</p>
<p>		    Aug 1996     Aug 1995	 pct</p>
<p>   Production   9,920.1	9,756.0	 +1.7</p>
<p>   Exports	5,364.2	5,256.1	 +2.1</p>
<p>   Imports	3,326.7	2,800.9	+18.8</p>
<p>   Ref receipts 8,031.4	7,339.4	 +9.4</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS (millions of cubic meters)</p>
<p>		    Aug 1996     Aug 1995	 pct</p>
<p>   Production  12,217.7     11,726.1	 +4.2</p>
<p>   Exports	6,697.3	6,572.0	 +1.9</p>
<p>   Canada sales 3,479.9	3,384.9	 +2.8</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL (thousands of cubic meters)</p>
<p>		  Jan/Aug 1996  Jan/Aug 1995   pct</p>
<p>   Production     76,443.9   75.511.4	+1.2</p>
<p>   Exports	  42,472.4   40,611.0	+4.6</p>
<p>   Imports	  26,737.2   22,829.4     +17.1</p>
<p>   Ref receipts   61,902.0   58,459.6	+5.9</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS (milions of Cubic meters)</p>
<p>   Production    100,937.0   97,910.0	+3.1</p>
<p>   Exports	  52,892.3   52,195.6	+1.3</p>
<p>   Canada sales   40,423.9   38.466.8	+4.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Canada sales include direct sales.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact David Roeske, Energy Section, (613) 951-3563.)</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
</text>
